<title>POLAND: KPW approves BRE-owned fund Skarbiec.</title>
<headline>KPW approves BRE-owned fund Skarbiec.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Polish Securities Commission (KPW) on Thursday cleared for operations mutual fund firm Skarbiec Towarzystwo Funduszy Powierniczych SA, 60-percent owned by Bank Rozwoju Eksportu SA (BRE), the fund's head said.</p>
<p>Zenon Slomski told a news conference on Thursday that the company, 40-percent owned by ADIC, in turn a subsidiary of Commerzbank and Bayerische Vereinsbank, sought to start selling units in two months.</p>
<p>He said the firm would administer three funds, one balanced, one stock-based and a money-market fund.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
